{start_of_verse}
I [G]left my old home in the mountains
And the only friends I ever [D]had
And [G]while I rambled this world [C]over
My [G]heart felt so [D]lonely and [G]sad
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]I’m going back to the [G]old home
Back to the place I love so [D]well
Where the [G]sweet waters flow and the [C]wildflowers grow
All a[D]round the old home on the [G]hill
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
I know that dear old mother’s waiting
Waiting alone on that hill
With the silver in her hair and a twinkle in her eye
In the old cabin home on the hill
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Years have gone by since I saw her
I’ve traveled many a mile
But tonight there’s a light in the window
And she’s waiting at the door with a smile
{end_of_verse}
